# [TVR](../wg/tvr.html)

## Summary

The Time-Variant Routing (TVR) Working Group met at IETF 127. The Working Group is nearing completion of its chartered work. Use cases have been published and the core requirements and data model specifications are currently in the RFC Editor Queue. The two remaining active working group drafts—`draft-ietf-tvr-applicability` and `draft-ietf-tvr-off-path-exposure`—are mature and ready for Working Group Last Call (WGLC). The chairs indicated plans to complete the remaining documents and target closing the working group around IETF 128. New extension work was proposed and directed toward destination working groups such as the Routing Working Group (RTGWG).

## Key Discussion Points

* **Working Group Status and Sunset Plan**
  * Jim Guichard presented the [0 - Chair slides](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-tvr-0-chair-slides-02).
  * The chairs noted that no new chartered work proposals have been brought forward.
  * Because core specifications are in the RFC Editor queue and remaining documents are mature, the chairs plan to finish the active drafts and target closing the TVR Working Group around IETF 128.

* **Applicability of TVR YANG Data Models**
  * Li Zhang presented updates on [`draft-ietf-tvr-applicability`](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-tvr-applicability-of-tvr-yang-data-models-00) ([slides](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-tvr-applicability-of-tvr-yang-data-models-00)).
  * Recent draft revisions (-01 and -02) aligned terminology with the TVR requirements draft, added operational sections on fallback and rollback mechanisms, corrected JSON examples to align with the latest schedule model, and adjusted reference classifications.
  * The draft is considered mature. No objections were raised against progressing the document to Working Group Last Call.

* **Using Off-Path Mechanisms for Exposing Time-Variant Routing Information**
  * Diego Lopez presented [`draft-ietf-tvr-off-path-exposure`](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-tvr-using-off-path-mechanisms-for-exposing-time-variant-routing-information-00) on behalf of Luis Contreras ([slides](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-tvr-using-off-path-mechanisms-for-exposing-time-variant-routing-information-00)).
  * The draft defines centralized off-path mechanisms to offload calculation and exposure of TVR information from individual network elements.
  * Recent changes polished document details and references. No objections were raised against moving this document to Working Group Last Call.

* **Lifecycle and State Extensions for TVR Schedule YANG Model**
  * Diego Lopez presented [Lifecycle and State Extensions for TVR Schedule YANG Model](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-tvr-lifecycle-and-state-extensions-for-tvr-schedule-yang-model-00) on behalf of Luis Contreras.
  * The proposal augments the base TVR schedule model to support administrative states (active, inactive, duplicated, pending) and lifecycle operational controls beyond simple time-interval triggers.
  * Rick Taylor expressed strong support for the work, noting its alignment with ongoing implementation engineering.
  * Jim Guichard noted that while the proposal is valuable, TVR will not remain open to charter new work. The Area Director and chairs confirmed that this extension work can be transitioned to the Routing Working Group (RTGWG) or Operations Area after TVR concludes.

* **Open Mic**
  * Daniel King proposed organizing an interop hackathon prior to working group closure (e.g., using the Teraflow SDN controller) and invited interested participants to coordinate on the mailing list.
  * A participant raised concerns regarding concluding the working group, noting potential intersections with satellite networking work in other groups. Jim Guichard and Li Zhang noted that satellite-related routing discussions can continue in forums such as the Space Research Group (Space RG) or RTGWG, and encouraged follow-up on the mailing list.

## Decisions and Action Items

* **Working Group Last Call (WGLC)**: Issue WGLC for `draft-ietf-tvr-applicability` and `draft-ietf-tvr-off-path-exposure`.
* **WG Sunset**: Plan for working group shutdown around IETF 128 following the progression of the active documents.
* **Work Transition**: Authors of TVR extension work (such as schedule lifecycle extensions) to transition drafts to RTGWG or OPS.

## Next Steps

* Chairs to issue Working Group Last Call calls on the TVR mailing list for `draft-ietf-tvr-applicability` and `draft-ietf-tvr-off-path-exposure`.
* Participants interested in a TVR hackathon prior to closure to coordinate planning on the working group mailing list.